\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Isolation of the estimated components. Spearman correlation between each estimated component and each ground truth, with 95\% intervals over label re-draws (real judge) or simulated worlds (calibrated). Isolation requires a strong diagonal and near-zero off-diagonal. The truth--truth column shows the two ground truths are themselves uncorrelated or anti-correlated, so the separation is not inherited from the world.}}{9}{table.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:isolation}{{4}{9}{Isolation of the estimated components. Spearman correlation between each estimated component and each ground truth, with 95\% intervals over label re-draws (real judge) or simulated worlds (calibrated). Isolation requires a strong diagonal and near-zero off-diagonal. The truth--truth column shows the two ground truths are themselves uncorrelated or anti-correlated, so the separation is not inherited from the world}{table.caption.25}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The judge's stated confidence is non-monotone in its error. By description tier (125 dice each): judge error is the mean Manhattan distance from the judge's predicted face distribution to the true one (0--2 scale). Stated confidence is the judge's self-reported certainty on its 0--100 scale, and variant spread is the standard deviation of the predicted face probabilities across three prompt paraphrases, in probability units (0.0002 means the paraphrases agree to the fourth decimal place).}}{9}{table.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:confidence}{{5}{9}{The judge's stated confidence is non-monotone in its error. By description tier (125 dice each): judge error is the mean Manhattan distance from the judge's predicted face distribution to the true one (0--2 scale). Stated confidence is the judge's self-reported certainty on its 0--100 scale, and variant spread is the standard deviation of the predicted face probabilities across three prompt paraphrases, in probability units (0.0002 means the paraphrases agree to the fourth decimal place)}{table.caption.26}{}}
